  "Question": "The general-term formula of an arithmetic sequence is a linear expression. How does the term change when \\(n\\) increases by 1?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "It becomes 2 times its original value",
    "B": "It must remain unchanged",
    "C": "It increases by the common difference",
    "D": "It becomes its square"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Adjacent terms differ by \\(d\\). Each time the index increases by 1, the common difference is added to the term.",
